2. LOCKED SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
======================================================================

A. Google Sheets
- Sole authoritative business database.
- Use the verified 255-tab post-cleanup baseline.
- 254 official Blueprint tables plus DBV5_FIELD_DICTIONARY_3074.
- Do not recreate the 46 deleted scratch tabs.
- Do not treat the 301-tab pre-cleanup snapshot as the current schema.
- Preserve unknown columns, extra columns, formulas, existing headers and
  existing data layout. Do not rename, delete, reorder, or rewrite headers.
- Match fields by exact live header name. Any alias mapping must be explicit,
  documented, and approved by the governing schema contract. Never silently
  guess a field match.
- The 94 core/workforce tables already hydrated by DictionaryHydrator.gs and
  WorkforceEngine.gs must be treated as existing hydrated tables, not
  re-created from stale KS_P3_FIELD_MAPPING snapshots.

B. Apps Script: SINGLE WRITE / POSTING OWNER
Apps Script is the only component allowed to perform governed business writes.
It owns:
- LockService-serialized ID allocation via IdAllocator.gs.
- nonce/idempotency handling via SafeWriter.gs.
- controlled writes and read-back verification.
- stock overdraft validation and inventory movements via InventoryEngine.gs.
- production and packaging governed workflows via
  ProductionAndPackagingEngine.gs.
- sales posting via SalesEngine.gs.
- paise-exact double-entry journal posting via AccountingEngine.gs.
- workforce payout separation via WorkforceEngine.gs.
- audit and exception records, including the required AuditLog format.

FastAPI must not independently allocate business IDs, append raw stock/ledger
rows, post accounting entries, or bypass Apps Script controls.

C. FastAPI: READ / QUERY / AUTH / GATEWAY
FastAPI owns:
- login/session authentication and token verification.
- exact role-based and field-level read permissions.
- filtered, paginated, searchable and date-range read APIs.
- response shaping and typed request/response schemas.
- request validation before forwarding.
- authenticated/signed forwarding of governed mutations to the approved
  Apps Script Web App / Execution API endpoints.
- forwarding the client nonce unchanged.
- interpreting Apps Script result/read-back confirmation and returning an
  accurate status to React.
- safe errors, exception logging, and short-lived read caches.
- immediate cache invalidation after confirmed successful writes.

FastAPI must never pretend a write succeeded merely because a request was
accepted or forwarded. A success response requires the Apps Script result and
required read-back verification. If the Apps Script response is ambiguous,
return a pending/unknown-safe state and do not invite blind duplicate posting.

D. React 18 + TypeScript + Vite: UI ONLY
- Read business records from FastAPI.
- Submit state changes to FastAPI with a unique client-generated nonce.
- Display the immutable business ID returned after Apps Script read-back.
- Do not write business records to localStorage, sessionStorage, IndexedDB,
  browser databases, or in-memory stores as a substitute for Sheets.
- Browser storage may hold only non-authoritative UI preferences and session
  authentication tokens, subject to the existing security design.
- Preserve unsaved form input in component memory when an API request fails;
  show that it was not saved and provide a safe retry using the same nonce for
  the same logical submission.
- Never generate a new nonce for an automatic retry of the same logical
  submission. A genuinely new transaction must receive a new nonce.

