4. FASTAPI BACKEND IMPLEMENTATION
======================================================================

4.1 Repository preservation
- Keep the existing FastAPI application structure and existing useful routers.
- Inspect existing routers before adding new ones. Extend existing modules
  instead of creating duplicates.
- Preserve existing route behaviour where it is compatible with the target
  architecture. Where a route must change, document old route, new route,
  compatibility handling, and affected frontend callers.
- Do not remove existing accounting, production, sales, inventory, workforce,
  attendance, visits, expenses, approvals, audit, closing, user, or reporting
  functionality without an explicit reason and replacement.

4.2 Google Sheets read adapter
- Centralise all Google Sheets reads through a single adapter/service layer.
- Use gspread/google-auth already present in the repository unless a
  documented technical reason requires otherwise.
- Read headers from Row 1 and resolve fields by exact header name.
- Never depend on fragile hard-coded column numbers when a header lookup is
  available.
- Support pagination, search, filtering, date ranges and controlled caching.
- Log missing sheet/header/configuration exceptions without silently returning
  fabricated empty business records.
- Distinguish an actually empty sheet from an unavailable sheet, permission
  error, timeout, malformed response, or missing header.
- Do not expose service-account credentials, tokens, or private configuration.

4.3 Apps Script write bridge
Create/extend one central Apps Script gateway client/service. All write routers
must use it. The bridge must:
- authenticate/sign requests using server-side secrets supplied through
  environment configuration;
- forward the client nonce unchanged;
- include actor identity, role, action, payload, request timestamp and
  correlation ID as required by the approved Apps Script contract;
- use timeouts and safe retry rules;
- avoid retrying non-idempotent requests with a different nonce;
- parse Apps Script result states and read-back confirmation;
- return the confirmed record ID and state;
- log correlation IDs, failure categories and safe diagnostic details;
- never log secrets or confidential employee/bank information.

Do not invent Apps Script function names or deployment URLs. Inspect the
supplied Apps Script source/manual for exact function names and contract. If
an endpoint or function is not present in the supplied materials, create a
clearly marked integration placeholder/configuration contract and report it
as a blocking dependency. Do not deploy or modify the live Apps Script project.

4.4 Required domain router coverage
Map and extend the existing routers to cover all required capabilities:
- Control/setup and business masters.
- Procurement and suppliers.
- Inventory and warehousing.
- Milling and production.
- Quality and food safety.
- Packaging and finished goods.
- Sales and customers.
- Marketplace/channel operations and settlements.
- Distribution and logistics.
- Finance and accounting.
- Workforce and payroll.
- Governance, compliance and audit.
