4.5 API versioning and contracts
- Use /api/v2 for new or upgraded contracts.
- Keep compatible existing routes where practical.
- Define typed Pydantic request/response models.
- Use Decimal for money values at API boundaries. Do not use binary floating
  point as the authoritative representation of money.
- Define explicit enums for workflow states.
- Use consistent error response structure with machine-readable error code,
  safe message, correlation ID, and retryability indicator.
- Provide server-side pagination metadata.
- Ensure API success/failure semantics reflect actual Sheets/Apps Script
  results.

4.6 Read caching
- Use short-lived cache only for reads.
- Invalidate affected cache keys immediately after confirmed successful writes.
- Do not cache confidential payroll/bank data in shared cache.
- Do not use cache as a write queue or source of truth.

4.7 Accounting and costing safeguards
- Enforce balanced debit/credit journal lines through Apps Script
  AccountingEngine.gs.
- Use integer paise in Apps Script and Decimal in FastAPI schemas.
- Respect open-period checks before posting.
- Do not hardcode unresolved GST rates, HSN decisions, inventory valuation
  method, overhead/labour allocation bases, or depreciation schedules.
- Keep unresolved policy inputs configurable and visibly marked
  PENDING_CA_APPROVAL.
- Do not enable automatic live financial posting for any policy that remains
  pending CA/Owner confirmation.
- Never silently change historic posted entries. Corrections must use linked
  reversals or approved adjustments.

