- Display the final immutable ID only after Apps Script confirms it.

Lot quality states:
PENDING_QC -> RELEASED / ON_HOLD / REJECTED.
Block packaging consumption and sales dispatch unless quality_status is
RELEASED. Enforce in both UI for user guidance and Apps Script for authority.
UI-only validation is not sufficient.

Retail SKU pack weights:
Enforce 200g, 500g and 1000g for retail SKU creation/packaging, matching the
approved ProductionAndPackagingEngine.gs rules. Do not reintroduce discontinued
pack sizes without an explicit approved master-data change.

Workforce separation:
- FIXED_EMPLOYEE: monthly salary structure -> PayrollRuns -> SalaryPayments.
- GIG_WORKER: daily piece/shift entry -> SUBMITTED -> VERIFIED -> PAID.
- Do not merge these payment flows or expose one category's fields in the
  other's workflow.

Workflow states must remain distinct. At minimum support the applicable
states: DRAFT, SUBMITTED, PENDING_QC, RELEASED, ON_HOLD, REJECTED, APPROVED,
POSTED, VERIFIED, PAID, REVERSED, FAILED. Do not collapse request, approval,
posting, payment, dispatch, settlement and reversal into one generic status.

